text.section:
If any prospective purchaser of a travel club membership is offered the opportunity to subscribe to or participate in any exchange program registered under the Virginia Real Estate Time-Share Act (§ 55.1-2200 et seq.), the public offering statement shall include as an exhibit or supplement, the disclosure document prepared by the exchange company in accordance with § 55.1-2219 and a brief narrative description of the exchange program which shall include the following:

A statement of whether membership or participation in the program is voluntary or mandatory;


The name and address of the exchange company together with the names of the principal officers and all directors of the exchange company;


A statement of whether the exchange company or any of its officers or directors are holders of a ten percent or greater interest in the travel club;


A statement of whether the travel club or any of its officers or directors are holders of a ten percent or greater interest in an exchange company;


A statement that the purchaser's contract with the exchange company is a contract separate and distinct from the purchaser's contract with the travel club; and


A brief narrative description of the procedure whereby exchanges are conducted.

The travel club shall amend the public offering statement to reflect any material change in the travel club membership. The travel club shall file with the Commissioner the public offering statement amended to reflect any material change. The Commissioner may at any time require the travel club to alter or supplement the form or substance of the public offering statement to assure full and fair disclosure to prospective purchasers.
			The following events shall not be deemed to be a material change necessitating an amendment to the public offering statement:

A change correcting spelling, grammar, omissions, or other similar errors not affecting the substance of the public offering statement;


A change in the fees, dues, or assessments of the purchasers or other similar recurring expense items;


A change which is an aspect or result of the orderly development, operation, or management of the travel club in accordance with the travel services agreement, including, without limitation, the addition or deletion of accommodations, transportation or other service related to travel;


A change resulting from the adoption of a new budget;


A change occurring in the issuance of an exchange company's updated annual report or disclosure documents provided upon its receipt by the travel club it shall commence distribution of same in lieu of all others; and


A change in the ownership of the travel club, provided the change affects less than an ownership interest of twenty percent.
